<title>POLAND: Skanska pays PLN 7.5 mln for Polish firm.</title>
<headline>Skanska pays PLN 7.5 mln for Polish firm.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Skane Grippen AB a unit of Skanska AB Holding paid 7.5 million zlotys for 75-percent of Polish furniture firm  Wolsztynska Fabryka Mebli Sp z oo, Poland's treasury ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement up to 20 percent of the shares were earmarked for employees and five percent for restitution claims.</p>
<p>Wolsztynska Fabryka Mebli employs 568 and had a net profit of 2.2 million zlotys in 1996.</p>
<p>Skane Gripen Aktiebolag pledged to increase the firm's capital by 7.5 million zlotys in the next five years, from current 3.4 million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
